| `tests.child_timeout_seconds` | integer | `600` | a whole number of seconds, 1 or more | `tests/integration/test_isolation_gate.py`, `tests/integration/test_scratch_root_gate.py`, the assertion-quality child in `tests/integration/test_copier_generation.py`, and `scripts/bounded_match.py`, which bounds commit-trailer backlog ids in `tests/integration/test_work_trailers.py`, forbidden phrases in `tests/integration/test_doc_drift.py` and dataset patterns in `evals/_scorers.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `tests.child_timeout_seconds` row | Sets how long one child process those tests start, a nested pytest session, a one-line Python or a configured regex batch, may run before `subprocess` kills it and the test fails. Absent, the test that reads it fails, naming this key. | the canary's per-step limit: `canary.step_timeout_minutes` | always |
